titis B virus X-protein</article-title><source>J. Hepatol.</source><year>1999</year><volume>31</volume><fpage>123</fpage><lpage>132</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10424292</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib11"><label>11.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Schaefer</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Properties of tumour suppressor p53 in murine hepatocyte lines transformed by hepatitis B virus X protein</article-title><source>J. Gen. Virol.</source><year>1998</year><comment><bold>79</bold> (Pt 4), 767&#x02013;777</comment></citation></ref><ref id="bib12"><label>12.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Tarn</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Differential immediate early gene expression in conditional hepatitis B virus pX-transforming versus nontransforming hepatocyte cell lines</article-title><source>J. Biol. Chem.</source><year>1999</year><volume>274</volume><fpage>2327</fpage><lpage>2336</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9890999</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib13"><label>13.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gottlob</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Hepatitis B virus X protein transcription activation domains are neither required nor sufficient for cell transformation</article-title><source>Cancer Res.</source><year>1998</year><volume>58</volume><fpage>3566</fpage><lpage>3570</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9721862</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib14"><label>14.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Birrer</surname><given-names>RB</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Hepatocellular carcinoma and hepatitis virus</article-title><source>Ann. Clin. Lab. Sci.</source><year>2003</year><volume>33</volume><fpage>39</fpage><lpage>54</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12661897</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib15"><label>15.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Groisman</surname><given-names>IJ</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Downregulation of DNA excision repair by the hepatitis B virus-x protein occurs in p53-proficient and p53-deficient cells</article-title><source>Carcinogenesis</source><year>1999</year><volume>20</volume><fpage>479</fpage><lpage>483</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10190565</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib16"><label>16.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Qiao</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Hepatitis B virus X protein increases expression of p21(Cip-1/WAF1/MDA6) and p27(Kip-1) in primary mouse hepatocytes, leading to reduced cell cycle progression</article-title><source>Hepatology</source><year>2001</year><volume>34</volume><fpage>906</fpage><lpage>917</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11679961</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib17"><label>17.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Miyazawa</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Expression of mesenchyme-specific gene HMGA2 in squamous cell carcinomas of the oral cavity</article-title><source>Cancer Res.</source><year>2004</year><volume>64</volume><fpage>2024</fpage><lpage>2029</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15026339</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib18"><label>18.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ng</surname><given-names>RK</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>cDNA microarray analysis of early gene expression profiles associated with hepatitis B virus X protein-med